From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/44] minimize: stale Firefox windows by when a title was
 left, live profile locks

Review fixes:
- A stale session window qualifies only when a live window left its
  selected title after that window's file was written, not merely had it
  in its history.
- A profile counts as running only when the pid in its lock link runs, so
  a crashed profile's file is not merged.
- A count is unlisted by the window's own profile file time, so an idle
  second profile does not hold it.
- A session file that cannot be read is left out; the others are used and
  it is read again next time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

